Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patch `12-quests-sheep-shearer-romeo-juliet` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`).

**Problem.** Sheep Shearer and Romeo & Juliet were not implemented, so Quest Helper and the quest list had nothing to track.

**Change.** Both quests on OpenRune's quest framework, with the OSRS progress varps Quest Helper reads:
- Sheep Shearer: varp 179 (`sheep`): 0 not started, 1 started, 1 + balls of wool handed in, 21 complete; Fred, The Thing and the hand-in.
- Romeo & Juliet: varp 144 (`rjquest`) with the OSRS stages 0-100; Romeo, Juliet, Father Lawrence, the Apothecary and the cadava potion.
- Adds `QuestTalkFixture` (a test fixture for dialogue-driven quest tests), which the other quest PRs (Witch's Potion, Goblin Diplomacy, Doric's Quest, Vampyre Slayer) build on.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: varp `sheep_shearer_state` 63712; varbits `sheep_shearer_progress` 63715, `sheep_shearer_saw_thing` 63716, `romeo_juliet_progress` 63717.

**Tests.** `SheepShearerInteractionTest`, `RomeoAndJulietInteractionTest` (`:content:quest:test`).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): buildCache pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble` pass, `test` pass, `integration` pass, boot pass (Server ready in 8.649210391s). `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Step values from Quest Helper (BSD) and the cache's quest dbrows. The patch does not record where each dialogue line came from; some of it may follow the OSRS Wiki transcripts.

**Caveats.**
- Overlaps #299 (Romeo & Juliet, open). Happy to drop ours or compare notes.

**Release note.** Sheep Shearer and Romeo & Juliet are playable, with the progress values Quest Helper reads.

